From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 07:19:20 +0000
Subject: fix: register the spare renderer before initializing it

SpareRenderProcessHostManagerImpl added a new spare to spare_rphs_ only
after RenderProcessHost::Init(), so RenderProcessHost::IsSpare() was
false while the process launched, including in
ContentBrowserClient::AppendExtraCommandLineSwitches(). Electron decides
a renderer's switches per WebContents there and needs to recognise the
spare, which has none. Push it onto the list first; nothing between the
two calls reads the list.

Upstreamed at https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8283216;
remove once it lands and rolls in.

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/spare_render_process_host_manager_impl.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/spare_render_process_host_manager_impl.cc
index 6895fdd5d7f8b165f4a0ab603b14400b87a5c24d..81b0abeb04d2497e468fa2b92b6c2d69b234ac49 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/spare_render_process_host_manager_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/spare_render_process_host_manager_impl.cc
@@ -558,8 +558,8 @@ RenderProcessHost* SpareRenderProcessHostManagerImpl::WarmupSpare(
       RenderProcessHostImpl::CreateSpareRenderProcessHost(
           browser_context, nullptr /* site_instance */);
   new_spare_rph->AddObserver(this);
-  new_spare_rph->Init();
   spare_rphs_.push_back(new_spare_rph);
+  new_spare_rph->Init();
 
   // Use the new timeout if there is no previous renderer or
   // the specified timeout will be triggered after the current timeout
@@ -1063,8 +1063,8 @@ void SpareRenderProcessHostManagerImpl::MaybeCreateExtraSpare() {
       RenderProcessHostImpl::CreateSpareRenderProcessHost(
           browser_context, nullptr /* site_instance */);
   new_spare_rph->AddObserver(this);
-  new_spare_rph->Init();
   spare_rphs_.push_back(new_spare_rph);
+  new_spare_rph->Init();
 }
 
 void SpareRenderProcessHostManagerImpl::OnMetricsHeartbeatTimerFired() {
